"Pizza as a service: IaaS = you get kitchen and make pizza yourself; PaaS = ready dough, you add toppings; SaaS = ordering a finished pizza.",
"EC2 (IaaS): you choose OS and install software. Elastic Beanstalk (PaaS): you upload code, AWS handles servers. Gmail/Salesforce (SaaS): you just use the app.",
["IaaS: virtual machines, storage, networking; you manage OS, runtime, apps (EC2, EBS, VPC).","PaaS: managed runtime; you manage code and data (Elastic Beanstalk, RDS-style platforms).","SaaS: complete application delivered over the internet (Gmail, Office 365).","Control decreases from IaaS → PaaS → SaaS; convenience increases.","FaaS/serverless (Lambda) is an extension of PaaS.","Responsibility split follows the model."],
["Responsibility matrix.","Examples of each.","IaaS vs PaaS vs SaaS table."],
["Classify a service.","Explain the responsibilities.","Choose a model for a scenario."],
["Calling RDS or Lambda IaaS — they are managed (PaaS-like).","Thinking SaaS needs you to manage servers."],
